<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Wogastisburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">631 or 632</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Wogastisburg was fought in 631 or 632 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samo</a> and the army of the Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagobert-i">Dagobert I</a>. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chronicle-of-fredegar">Chronicle of Fredegar</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> besieged the stronghold for three days before being routed and fleeing, leaving their camp behind. The victory secured Samo's realm; the site, probably in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> or nearby, has not been identified.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-wogastisburg.jpg" alt="Battle of Wogastisburg" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Věnceslav Černý · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:V%C4%9Bnceslav_%C4%8Cern%C3%BD_-_Bitva_u_Vogastisburku_roku_630.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
